{
  "about": "Dataflows, a node of each, and the spec its scenario chips, and the chip of the dataset its inputs are stacked in, [!! inputs !!], resolve to from the dataflow's boxes, nodes and edges: each wired input's label is the box its feeding node is in, ranked by the dataflow's list of boxes, or its node's title, renamed header or type for a node in no box, in grey. Read by src/tests/NotebookConvertor.test.ts, as the notebook export writes each spec, and by utk_curio/backend/tests/test_execution/test_scenario_chips.py, as the server resolves a node's references for a run and for the agents' check (WorkflowSpec.node_code). A case may carry \"labels\", each template's label by its unversioned id, which name an untitled node as its header does: the browser reads them from the node registry, the server from the project's templates.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a chart's chips list the boxes in the order the dataflow lists them, then an input from no box by its node's title, in grey",
      "grammar": "vega-lite",
      "node": "chart",
      "dataflow": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "id": "base",
            "type": "curio.builtin/computation-analysis",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "content": "return input_0\n",
            "title": "Shade"
          },
          {
            "id": "tall",
            "type": "curio.builtin/computation-analysis",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "content": "return input_0\n",
            "title": "Shade"
          },
          {
            "id": "survey",
            "type": "curio.builtin/computation-analysis",
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "content": "return input_0\n",
            "title": "Roof survey"
          },
          {
            "id": "chart",
            "type": "curio.builtin/vis-vega",
            "x": 700,
            "y": 0,
            "content": "{\"data\": {\"name\": \"[!! inputs !!]\"}, \"mark\": \"bar\", \"encoding\": {\"x\": {\"field\": [!! inputs.scenario_name !!], \"type\": \"nominal\", \"sort\": [!! scenario order !!]}, \"y\": {\"field\": \"sunlight\", \"type\": \"quantitative\", \"aggregate\": \"mean\"}, \"color\": {\"field\": \"scenario_name\", \"type\": \"nominal\", \"scale\": [!! scenario colors !!]}}}"
          }
        ],
        "edges": [
          {
            "id": "e-base-chart",
            "source": "base",
            "target": "chart",
            "sourceHandle": "out",
            "targetHandle": "in"
          },
          {
            "id": "e-tall-chart",
            "source": "tall",
            "target": "chart",
            "sourceHandle": "out",
            "targetHandle": "in_1"
          },
          {
            "id": "e-survey-chart",
            "source": "survey",
            "target": "chart",
            "sourceHandle": "out",
            "targetHandle": "in_2"
          }
        ],
        "scenarios": [
          {
            "id": "s-tall",
            "name": "Twice as tall",
            "color": "#e76f51",
            "nodes": [
              "tall"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "s-base",
            "name": "Baseline",
            "color": "#2a9d8f",
            "nodes": [
              "base"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "expected": "{\"data\": {\"name\": \"inputs\"}, \"mark\": \"bar\", \"encoding\": {\"x\": {\"field\": \"scenario_name\", \"type\": \"nominal\", \"sort\": [\"Twice as tall\", \"Baseline\", \"Roof survey\"]}, \"y\": {\"field\": \"sunlight\", \"type\": \"quantitative\", \"aggregate\": \"mean\"}, \"color\": {\"field\": \"scenario_name\", \"type\": \"nominal\", \"scale\": {\"domain\": [\"Twice as tall\", \"Baseline\", \"Roof survey\"], \"range\": [\"#e76f51\", \"#2a9d8f\", \"#8a8f98\"]}}}}"
    },
